# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Reproducibility policy (reviewer 3, Q7 asked for code + checkpoints + eval
# scripts + reward implementations). The rule here:
#
#   COMMITTED  — all code, all configs, the experiment manifest, and every
#                small result artifact a reader needs to rebuild the tables
#                and figures: results.json, epoch_sweep.csv, history.csv,
#                config.json, generated SMILES, tables and figures.
#   IGNORED    — only things that are large and regenerable: model
#                checkpoints, the datasets, per-epoch images, logs.
#
# Checkpoints are released separately (see README "Artifact release"), not via
# git, because a 300-epoch run writes ~850 files.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Large regenerable artifacts ---
*.ckpt
*.pt
*.pth
*.npy
*.sparsedataset
data/gdb9.sdf
data/gdb9.sdf.csv
data/*.smi
slurm_logs/
**/train/img_dir/
**/train/log_dir/
logs/

# --- Result trees: ignore by default, then re-include the small artifacts ---
results/*
!results/runs/
results/runs/*
!results/runs/*/
!results/tables/
!results/latent_analysis/
!results/manuscript_v1/
!results/v1_reference/
results/runs/*/train/
!results/runs/*/config.json
!results/runs/*/history.csv
!results/runs/*/eval/
!results/runs/*/eval/results.json
!results/runs/*/eval/epoch_sweep.csv
!results/runs/*/eval/smiles_*.txt

# --- Editor / OS / Python noise ---
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.egg-info/

# --- Reference code kept locally, not redistributed ---
original_kao_code/
archived/
misc/
